From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SR2 Launcher <sr2-launcher@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] app: Slime Rancher 2 settings built in

GameRecommendations.slimeRancher2, recognised by Steam App ID 1657630, the
"Slime Rancher 2" Steam folder or SlimeRancher2.exe: the config the game ran
with on an iPhone 16 Pro Max (2026-11-09 and 11-10), plus two diagnostics-only
lines: MADEIRA_PROBES = light (no thread-suspending samplers) and
MADEIRA_LEAN_DIAG = 1 (the pool warmer's region sweep and zone check once a
minute); 960x540 with MetalFX 2x, fit, a 30 FPS limit and no launch arguments
(which removes -force-d3d12).

GameRecommendation gains two optional fields, arguments and metalFXUpscale,
which Reset to Recommended and first sight copy to the library entry.

This build exists for the game, so an entry already in the library takes the
whole list once per list version, also over a config of its own (what Reset
to Recommended does); the replaced config and arguments go to the log first.
After that the player's changes stay until the list's version rises.

check-game-recommendations.py knows the list, and its Swift fixture checks
recognition, the one-time takeover, that later changes stay, and Reset.
The fixture also takes upstream's fix df04bf0 (#564) for its Garry's Mod
case, which expected hl2.exe to be recognised and failed on v0.2.0 itself,
and counts 52 Steam titles and 78 lists.
