+    /// Slime Rancher 2 (Steam App ID 1657630): the game SR2 Launcher is built for. Device-tested on an
+    /// iPhone 16 Pro Max (A18 Pro, 8 GB), 2026-11-09 and 11-10, on Madeira 0.2.0. All but the last
+    /// two lines are the config those runs used, less their FEX_MEMCPYSETTSOENABLED = 0 (FEX logged
+    /// memcpyset=false without it: its default). donor-pool-guard with the 2 GB donor pool and 4 GB swap
+    /// tier (SR2Launcher.seedDefaults) lets the world load inside the 6 GB an app gets; the FPS
+    /// governor holds the CPU near 2 W so the thermal clamp comes later. The last two lines are
+    /// diagnostics only: MADEIRA_PROBES = light leaves the counters ([xp], [xp-t]) and stops the
+    /// samplers that suspend the game's threads; MADEIRA_LEAN_DIAG = 1 (as in Horizon Forbidden West's
+    /// tested lists) runs the pool warmer's region sweep and zone check once a minute, not every 2-10 s.
+    /// 960x540 with MetalFX 2x and a 30 FPS limit is the display setup of those runs; the game's
+    /// Options page stays white at that size (1280x720 shows it). No launch arguments: with
+    /// -force-d3d12 and a D3D11On12 bridge the game ran on madeira-d3d12 at 9-15 FPS against
+    /// 28-30 on DXMT.
+    static let slimeRancher2AppID = 1657630
+    static let slimeRancher2 = GameRecommendation(
+        id: "slime-rancher-2", title: "Slime Rancher 2", version: 1,
+        config: """
+        # Madeira's recommended settings for Slime Rancher 2 (SR2 Launcher's list).
+        # Reset to Recommended, at the bottom of the game's settings, brings them back.
+        env.MADEIRA_EC_HOOK_TRACE = 0
+        donor-pool-guard = 1
+        env.FEX_VECTORTSOENABLED = 0
+        env.MADEIRA_FPS_GOV_MW = 2000
+        env.MADEIRA_FPS_GOV_MAX = 30
+        env.MADEIRA_FPS_GOV_MIN = 20
+        env.MADEIRA_PROBES = light
+        env.MADEIRA_LEAN_DIAG = 1
+        """,
+        fpsMode: 3, resolution: "960x540", display: "fit", arguments: "", metalFXUpscale: 2)
+
     /// The Escapists 2 (Steam App ID 641990). Device-tested on an iPhone 17 Pro Max (2026-10-30, "works perfect").
     /// A 32-bit Unity game on its own old mono.dll: Mono's XCHG code patches at unaligned addresses faulted through
     /// the JIT pool's alias, so its code memory stays plain read/write (MADEIRA_WOW_RWX_PLAIN).
